From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:28:52 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: SyncSocket pipes in the LOCAL namespace

A UWP app may create named pipes only under the LOCAL folder of the pipe
namespace; base::SyncSocket::CreatePair hit CHECK(handle_a.is_valid())
when a page started audio (opening a video).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 base/sync_socket_win.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/base/sync_socket_win.cc b/base/sync_socket_win.cc
index 77bc8e15b180532b4d20cd33275155bd9d41a7d9..93d78531907937bd84f2f6d69dd8185038e6b69c 100644
--- a/base/sync_socket_win.cc
+++ b/base/sync_socket_win.cc
@@ -26,7 +26,15 @@ namespace {
 // IMPORTANT: do not change how this name is generated because it will break
 // in sandboxed scenarios as we might have by-name policies that allow pipe
 // creation. Also keep the secure random number generation.
+#if defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
+// Windows 10 Mobile: a UWP app may create pipes only in the pipe namespace's
+// LOCAL folder (CreateNamedPipe fails otherwise), and this pair never leaves
+// the process.
+const wchar_t kPipeNameFormat[] =
+    L"\\\\.\\pipe\\LOCAL\\chrome.sync.%u.%u.%lu";
+#else
 const wchar_t kPipeNameFormat[] = L"\\\\.\\pipe\\chrome.sync.%u.%u.%lu";
+#endif
 const size_t kPipePathMax = std::size(kPipeNameFormat) + (3 * 10) + 1;
 
 // To avoid users sending negative message lengths to Send/Receive
